C. Threshold Setting for Quality Assessment
An important step in constructing the quality assessment system is setting the thresholds for signal quality levels. Typically, these thresholds are determined based on past experience with signal quality scores. However, in our algorithm, the purpose of signal quality assessment is not solely to differentiate between the estimated HR and the GT, but rather to identify the most reliable HR frequencies and signal segments for subsequent algorithm optimization. This allows signals with initially large errors to find the dominant HR frequency at certain moments. To set the thresholds, we selected videos of all participants in a stationary state and scored the signals from 42 regions at each moment in the video. We chose these videos because signals in stationary videos exhibit higher quality scores in extreme cases, making it easier to observe the differences between signals with low scores but dominant frequencies that match the GT, and signals with high scores but dominant frequencies that do not match the GT.

